.TH GETDENTS64 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getdents64 \- read Linux directory records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <dirent.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t getdents64(int " descriptor ", void* " buffer ", size_t " byte_count ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads variable\-length Linux x86\-64 directory records from an open directory
descriptor into the writable buffer. The buffer must have at least
.I byte_count
bytes. The count must be between 0 and 4294967295 inclusive; values outside
that range fail with
.BR EINVAL .
The kernel can reject a buffer too small for the next record.
Use
.BR dirent64_next (3crunch)
to decode each returned buffer; records and entry order are filesystem\-specific.
Repeated calls continue from the descriptor's current directory position.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the byte count on success, zero at end of directory, or \-1 with
positive Linux
.B errno
on failure. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dirent64_next (3crunch),
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR getdents64 (2)
